.TH SOC-DEREGISTER 1 "October 2026" "OTA-Pulse" "OTA-Pulse Manual"
.SH NAME
soc-deregister \- deregister this device from the OTA-Pulse backend
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B soc-deregister
[\fB\-\-force\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Notifies the backend that the device is removed and deletes the local credentials. The device registers
again at the next start if a provisioning token is still present. Needs root.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-force
Do not ask for confirmation.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR soc-ctl (1),
.BR socmond (1)
